  "notes": "Prices in USD per 1M tokens, standard (non-batch) API tier. Tiered-price models record the base (lowest) tier with the higher tier in the model's note field. Retired models excluded; deprecated-but-available models included. Collected Monday 2026-09-07. The previous file was collected Tuesday 2026-09-01, one day off its Monday slot, so the gap here is 6 days rather than 7. Tracked scope follows the set established on 2026-07-16 so week-over-week deltas stay meaningful. ZERO price moves on the 43 rows carried over from 2026-09-01 — a second consecutive all-unchanged week for the carried set, across all six providers. Every change this week is an arrival: four new models entered the set, taking it from 43 rows to 47, and none left. Anthropic added Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 at $10/$50, matching the Fable 5 and Mythos 5 base rates they sit beside; the departure is in caching, where both price cache hits and refreshes at 0.025x base input ($0.25/MTok) against the 0.1x multiplier every other Claude model uses, and the page states the multiplier explicitly in a footnote. That is the first split in the Claude cache-read multiplier since this series began. OpenAI added gpt-6-astra at $10.00/$50.00 with a $20.00/$75.00 long-context tier, landing exactly on the $10.00/$50.00 that Claude Fable 5 and Claude Fable 5.1 charge. It is the most expensive OpenAI row in the set outside the $30.00/$180.00 pro tier (gpt-5.5-pro, gpt-5.4-pro), which remains the ceiling. Google added gemini-3.8-flash at $0.75/$3.75, the same introductory rate and the same 2026-12-31 expiry already carried by gemini-3.7-flash and gemini-3.6-flash, which takes the count of Gemini rows scheduled to double on 2027-01-01 from two to three. Forward signals still standing on the pages: the 2026-11-21 promotional expiry on gpt-5.6-sol ($4.00/$20.00), and the 2026-12-31 introductory expiry on gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.7-flash and gemini-3.6-flash. Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 5 note is unchanged from 2026-09-01: the $2/$10 rate \"is now the standard price\" and the cancelled increase to $3/$15 remains cancelled. Still observed and still out of the rows, unchanged from 2026-09-01: Mistral's resale of Z.ai GLM 5.2 at $1.40/$4.40 with cached input $0.14, Ministral 3 in three sizes (3B $0.10/$0.10, 8B $0.15/$0.15, 14B $0.20/$0.20), and DeepSeek's deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp at v4-flash rates. The GLM 5.2 scope question — whether a third-party model resold on a tracked provider's API belongs in this series — remains open for 기웅.",
